; Wait until a key is pressed
;
; Enables interrupts and halts until the next frame interrupt, then reads all eight keyboard half-rows at once (port
; $FE with a zero high byte) and repeats until one of the five key bits shows a pressed key. Called by the main loop
; (#R$85FC), the ending (#R$887B) and #R$9C52.
; .
; Hardware: HALT for the frame interrupt; reads the ULA keyboard port $FE.
@label=WaitKeyPress
c$A1C3 EI            ;
 $A1C4 HALT          ;
 $A1C5 XOR A         ; A = 0 selects every half-row
@isub=IN A,(ULA_PORT)
 $A1C6 IN A,($FE)    ;
 $A1C8 CPL           ;
@isub=AND KEY_BITS
 $A1C9 AND $1F       ; bits set = keys down
 $A1CB JR Z,$A1C3    ;
 $A1CD RET           ;
